B.bz_=s([A.c5T(),A.c5N(),A.c62(),A.c60(),A.c5V(),A.c5U(),A.c5W()],t.ox)
B.bjK=s(["What is menopause?","What is the difference between perimenopause and menopause?","Am I in perimenopause?","What is postmenopause?"],t.s)
B.bqH=s(["perimenopause","stages","transition","postmenopause"],t.s)
B.bBa=s(["Perimenopause is the time leading up to menopause, when the ovaries slowly make less oestrogen and progesterone. Periods often become irregular, and symptoms like hot flashes, poor sleep or mood changes can start.","Menopause itself is one moment: 12 months in a row without a period. In Canada it happens at about 51 on average. Everything after that is called postmenopause.","The transition most often begins between 45 and 55 and usually lasts several years, about seven on average, though it can be shorter or longer."],t.s)
B.aLn=s([B.a0x,B.Cq,B.a0t,B.a0g],t.P)
B.bR=s([],t.G)
B.alP=new A.bO("what-is-perimenopause",B.lD,"What is perimenopause?",B.bjK,B.bqH,B.bBa,null,B.aLn,B.bR)
B.boH=s(["Is there a test for menopause?","Do I need a blood test to know if I am in menopause?","What are the signs of menopause?"],t.s)
B.bbB=s(["signs","test","fsh","diagnosed","started"],t.s)
B.bmY=s(["For most women over 45, menopause is recognised from your periods and symptoms rather than a test: it has happened once you have gone 12 months without a period.","Hormone blood tests (like FSH) go up and down a lot during perimenopause, so a single result often can't say where you are. Doctors mostly use them for younger women or when the picture is unclear.","Common early signs are changes in your cycle, hot flashes or night sweats, trouble sleeping, mood changes and vaginal dryness."],t.s)
B.bnI=s([B.a0w,B.a0F,B.uQ],t.P)
B.alH=new A.bO("am-i-in-menopause",B.lD,"How do I know if I am in menopause?",B.boH,B.bbB,B.bmY,"If your periods stop or symptoms start before 45, or you are not sure what is going on, it is worth a visit.",B.bnI,B.bR)
B.boI=s(["My periods are irregular","Why are my periods heavier?","Skipped period perimenopause"],t.s)
B.bex=s(["period","periods","irregular","heavy","cycle","spotting"],t.s)
B.bk1=s(["Yes, changing periods are usually the first sign of perimenopause. They can come closer together or further apart, be lighter or heavier, and you may skip some.","Keeping a simple note of dates and flow (the Journal works for this) makes it easier to describe to your doctor."],t.s)
B.aRd=s([B.Cq,B.Cg],t.P)
B.Eh=new A.fv(B.oq,null,4,"iron")
B.pg=new A.fv(null,"ferritin",16,"ferritin")
B.bet=s([B.Eh,B.pg],t.G)
B.alI=new A.bO("periods-changing",B.lD,"Is it normal for my periods to change?",B.boI,B.bex,B.bk1,"See your doctor for very heavy bleeding (soaking a pad or tampon every hour or two), periods lasting more than about a week, bleeding between periods or after sex, or any bleeding once periods have stopped for 12 months.",B.aRd,B.bet)
B.bwC=s(["Spotting after my periods stopped","Postmenopausal bleeding","Bleeding after a year with no period"],t.s)
B.bzH=s(["postmenopausal","spotting","bleeding","bleed"],t.s)
B.bby=s(["Any bleeding or spotting once you have gone 12 months without a period should be checked by a doctor, even if it is light or happens only once.","Most of the time the cause is something simple, like thin, dry tissue or a polyp, but bleeding after menopause can sometimes be an early sign of cancer of the uterus, which is very treatable when found early."],t.s)
B.bfK=s([B.Cg,B.Cv],t.P)
B.am3=new A.bO("bleeding-after-menopause",B.lD,"I have bleeding after menopause. Is that normal?",B.bwC,B.bzH,B.bby,"Book an appointment soon rather than waiting to see if it stops.",B.bfK,B.bR)
B.bgu=s(["When will hot flashes stop?","Will this ever end?"],t.s)
B.bfU=s(["long","last","years","stop","end"],t.s)
B.bbW=s(["It is different for everyone. Hot flashes and night sweats often last several years, around seven on average, and some women have them for longer. Others have very few.","Many symptoms, like brain fog and sleep trouble, tend to ease after the transition. Some changes, like vaginal dryness and bone loss, can continue, which is why looking after bones, heart and pelvic health matters long term."],t.s)
B.ben=s([B.oG,B.Cu,B.a0a],t.P)
B.alU=new A.bO("how-long-symptoms",B.lD,"How long do menopause symptoms last?",B.bgu,B.bfU,B.bbW,"If symptoms are affecting your work, sleep or relationships, you do not have to wait them out: there are effective treatments.",B.ben,B.bR)
B.byn=s(["How do I stop hot flushes?","Ways to cool down during a hot flash","Natural remedies for hot flashes"],t.s)
B.bd7=s(["flash","flashes","flush","flushes","heat","cool"],t.s)
B.bA9=s(["Simple things help many women: dress in layers you can take off, keep a fan or cold drink nearby, and notice your own triggers. Common ones are alcohol, caffeine, spicy food, hot drinks, stress and warm rooms.","Slow, paced breathing when a flash starts can take the edge off (the hot flash breathing practice in Mindfulness is made for this). Cognitive behavioural therapy (CBT) and clinical hypnosis also have good evidence.","For flashes that really get in the way, hormone therapy is the most effective treatment, and there are non-hormonal prescription options too. These are worth a conversation with your doctor."],t.s)
B.bgS=s([B.Co,B.oG,B.Cs],t.P)
B.a4d=new A.fv(null,null,23,"mindfulness")
B.Ap=s([B.a4d],t.G)
B.alo=new A.bO("hot-flashes",B.eA,"What helps with hot flashes?",B.byn,B.bd7,B.bA9,"Talk to your doctor if hot flashes disturb your sleep or daily life.",B.bgS,B.Ap)
B.bAw=s(["I wake up soaked","Sweating at night","Too hot in bed"],t.s)
B.bmN=s(["sweat","sweats","sweating","soaked","drenched","night"],t.s)
B.bgA=s(["Night sweats are hot flashes that happen while you sleep. A cool bedroom, a fan, light breathable sheets and nightwear, and layers you can throw off all help.","Keep cold water by the bed, and try to avoid alcohol, big meals and spicy food in the evening, since they are common triggers.","If they wake you most nights, the same treatments that help hot flashes (including hormone therapy) usually help night sweats."],t.s)
B.bi4=s([B.oG,B.a0e],t.P)
B.am1=new A.bO("night-sweats",B.eA,"How can I cope with night sweats?",B.bAw,B.bmN,B.bgA,"Night sweats with fever, weight loss you can't explain, or that started outside the usual menopause years should be checked.",B.bi4,B.bR)
B.bvx=s(["Does spicy food cause hot flashes?","Does wine make hot flashes worse?"],t.s)
B.bqB=s(["trigger","triggers","spicy","wine","alcohol","coffee"],t.s)
B.aZh=s(["The most common triggers are alcohol (especially red wine), caffeine, spicy food and hot drinks. Smoking and stress can make them worse too.","Triggers are personal. Noting when flashes happen in the Journal for a week or two, alongside your food log, can show whether any of these matter for you."],t.s)
B.bc3=s([B.uS,B.oG],t.P)
B.am4=new A.bO("hot-flash-triggers",B.eA,"Which foods trigger hot flashes?",B.bvx,B.bqB,B.aZh,null,B.bc3,B.bR)
B.bit=s(["Memory problems during menopause","I can't concentrate","Trouble finding words"],t.s)
B.bCi=s(["fog","memory","forget","forgetful","concentrate","focus"],t.s)
B.bC4=s(["Brain fog, forgetfulness and trouble concentrating are common in perimenopause. Changing hormones play a part, and so do poor sleep and stress. For most women it improves after the transition.","Things that help: better sleep (and treating night sweats that break it), regular movement, lists and reminders, and doing one thing at a time."],t.s)
B.bBf=s([B.lC,B.uQ],t.P)
B.alJ=new A.bO("brain-fog",B.eA,"Why do I have brain fog and forget things?",B.bit,B.bCi,B.bC4,"If memory problems are getting worse, worrying you or your family, or come with other changes, see your doctor.",B.bBf,B.bR)
B.bdb=s(["Stiff joints in the morning","Achy muscles menopause"],t.s)
B.aZ9=s(["joint","joints","ache","aches","achy","stiff","stiffness"],t.s)
B.brw=s(["Aching, stiff joints are a common and often overlooked menopause symptom, as oestrogen helps with inflammation and joint comfort.","Gentle regular movement, strength work, stretching, staying at a healthy weight and sleep all help. Warmth can ease morning stiffness."],t.s)
B.aLa=s([B.lC,B.a0L],t.P)
B.w6=new A.fv(null,null,21,"movement")
B.AK=s([B.w6],t.G)
B.amc=new A.bO("joint-aches",B.eA,"Why do my joints ache?",B.bdb,B.aZ9,B.brw,"See your doctor if a joint is red, hot or swollen, if pain is severe, or if it does not improve.",B.aLa,B.AK)
B.bn6=s(["Heart palpitations","Pounding heart at night"],t.s)
B.bbF=s(["palpitations","racing","flutter","fluttering","pounding"],t.s)
B.bhn=s(["Palpitations (a racing, pounding or fluttering heartbeat) are common around menopause, often with hot flashes. Caffeine, alcohol, stress and poor sleep can set them off.","They are usually harmless, but because heart disease risk rises after menopause, new palpitations are worth mentioning to your doctor."],t.s)
B.bhY=s([B.a0E,B.uT,B.uP],t.P)
B.alM=new A.bO("palpitations",B.eA,"Why does my heart race or flutter?",B.bn6,B.bbF,B.bhn,"Call 911 if palpitations come with chest pain, shortness of breath, fainting or feeling very unwell. Otherwise see your doctor if they are new, frequent or last a long time.",B.bhY,B.bR)
B.aLm=s(["My migraines are worse","More headaches lately"],t.s)
B.boA=s(["headache","headaches","migraine","migraines"],t.s)
B.bio=s(["Yes. Shifting hormone levels can make headaches and migraines more frequent in perimenopause. For many women who had hormone-linked migraines, they ease after menopause.","Regular meals, enough water, steady sleep, and keeping an eye on caffeine and alcohol help. A headache diary can show patterns."],t.s)
B.b7I=s([B.a0B,B.a0y,B.oH],t.P)
B.alZ=new A.bO("headaches",B.eA,"Can menopause cause headaches or migraines?",B.aLm,B.boA,B.bio,"Get help right away (call 911) for a sudden, very severe headache, or one with weakness, confusion, trouble speaking or a drooping face. See your doctor if headaches change or get worse.",B.b7I,B.bR)
B.bfh=s(["Itchy skin menopause","Hair loss menopause","Dry eyes"],t.s)
B.bvN=s(["skin","itchy","dry","hair","thinning","eyes","nails"],t.s)
B.biq=s(["Lower oestrogen means skin makes less collagen and oil, so dryness, itchiness and thinner skin are common. Hair can thin too, and some women notice dry eyes.","A gentle fragrance-free moisturiser, sunscreen, enough protein and healthy fats, and drinking enough water help."],t.s)
B.bn4=s([B.lC,B.a0v,B.a0f,B.a0q],t.P)
B.Ej=new A.fv(null,"tsh",20,"tsh")
B.bp2=s([B.pg,B.Ej],t.G)
B.am7=new A.bO("skin-hair",B.eA,"Why is my skin dry and my hair thinning?",B.bfh,B.bvN,B.biq,"See your doctor for sudden or patchy hair loss, or itching with a rash; it can be checked for things like thyroid or iron problems.",B.bn4,B.bp2)
B.bvU=s(["Menopause belly","How do I lose weight during menopause?","Why is my weight going up?"],t.s)
B.bhD=s(["weight","belly","middle","waist","gain","lose","fat"],t.s)
B.bCI=s(["Lower oestrogen shifts where the body stores fat, towards the waist, and muscle is slowly lost with age, which lowers the calories you burn. Poor sleep and stress add to it.","What helps most is building and keeping muscle (strength work twice a week and protein at each meal), plenty of fibre, regular activity, and good sleep. Small steady changes work better than strict diets."],t.s)
B.bqF=s([B.a0A,B.uR,B.uV],t.P)
B.w4=new A.fv(B.e0,null,0,"protein")
B.pf=new A.fv(B.dK,null,3,"fiber")
B.ph=new A.fv(null,null,22,"strength")
B.be6=s([B.w4,B.pf,B.ph],t.G)
B.alX=new A.bO("weight-gain",B.eA,"Why am I gaining weight around my middle?",B.bvU,B.bhD,B.bCI,null,B.bqF,B.be6)
B.biA=s(["Bloating and gas","Constipation menopause","Upset tummy"],t.s)
B.bul=s(["bloat","bloated","bloating","gas","constipation","constipated","digestion"],t.s)
B.bec=s(["Bloating is common around menopause, as hormone changes affect digestion and fluid. Constipation can add to it.","Raising fibre slowly (with more water), eating regular meals, moving every day and noticing foods that bother you (fizzy drinks, some beans or onions, sweeteners like sorbitol) often help."],t.s)
B.biB=s([B.a09,B.a0Q,B.Cf],t.P)
B.PP=s([B.pf],t.G)
B.alF=new A.bO("bloating",B.eA,"Why do I feel bloated?",B.biA,B.bul,B.bec,"See your doctor if bloating is there most days for three weeks or more, or comes with weight loss, blood in your stool, changes in bowel habits or feeling full quickly.",B.biB,B.PP)
B.bpN=s(["Light-headed","Feeling faint"],t.s)
B.bdV=s(["dizzy","dizziness","lightheaded","faint","vertigo"],t.s)
B.bc0=s(["Some women feel dizzy or light-headed around menopause, sometimes with hot flashes or palpitations. Not drinking enough, skipping meals, standing up quickly and low iron can also cause it."],t.s)
B.aTz=s([B.a0j,B.oH],t.P)
B.Ei=new A.fv(null,"hemoglobin",17,"hemoglobin")
B.ast=s([B.Ei,B.pg],t.G)
B.alV=new A.bO("dizziness",B.eA,"Why do I feel dizzy?",B.bpN,B.bdV,B.bc0,"Call 911 if dizziness comes with chest pain, a drooping face, weakness or trouble speaking. See your doctor if it keeps happening.",B.aTz,B.ast)
B.biO=s(["I can't sleep","Insomnia during menopause","Trouble falling asleep"],t.s)
B.bng=s(["sleep","insomnia","asleep","bedtime","rest"],t.s)
B.bCf=s(["Sleep problems are very common in menopause, from night sweats, needing the bathroom, worry and hormone changes.","Steady habits help: the same wake-up time every day, a cool, dark bedroom, no caffeine after lunch, less alcohol, daylight and movement during the day, and winding down without screens.","Cognitive behavioural therapy for insomnia (CBT-I) is the first treatment experts recommend for long-term insomnia, and it works well. Treating night sweats often helps sleep too."],t.s)
B.bwk=s([B.Cp,B.Cl,B.a0N,B.a0O],t.P)
B.alQ=new A.bO("sleep-better",B.jC,"How can I sleep better?",B.biO,B.bng,B.bCf,"See your doctor if poor sleep lasts more than a few weeks, or if you snore loudly or stop breathing in your sleep (sleep apnoea becomes more common after menopause).",B.bwk,B.AK)
B.bz0=s(["Waking up during the night","I wake up and can't get back to sleep"],t.s)
B.bfj=s(["wake","waking","awake","3am","night"],t.s)
B.beM=s(["Waking in the night is a classic menopause complaint. Night sweats, a full bladder, a racing mind and lighter sleep with age all play a part.","If you can't get back to sleep after about 20 minutes, get up and do something quiet in dim light until you feel sleepy. Slow breathing or a body scan can help. Cutting back on fluids and alcohol in the evening helps with bathroom trips."],t.s)
B.by3=s([B.Cp,B.Cl,B.a0n],t.P)
B.ami=new A.bO("waking-at-night",B.jC,"Why do I wake up at 3 am?",B.bz0,B.bfj,B.beM,"Restless, uncomfortable legs at night, or loud snoring, are worth mentioning to your doctor.",B.by3,B.Ap)
B.bdM=s(["Mood swings menopause","I feel on edge","Anxiety during perimenopause"],t.s)
B.bej=s(["anxiety","anxious","irritable","mood","moods","swings","angry","worry","panic"],t.s)
B.buj=s(["Mood changes, anxiety and irritability are common in perimenopause. Changing hormones affect brain chemicals, and poor sleep and life stress add up.","Regular movement, time outdoors, connecting with people, cutting back on alcohol and caffeine, and calming practices like slow breathing help many women. CBT works well for anxiety and for menopause symptoms."],t.s)
B.aZm=s([B.lC,B.Cw,B.a0b,B.a07],t.P)
B.bqo=s([B.a4d,B.w6],t.G)
B.am9=new A.bO("anxiety-mood",B.jC,"Why do I feel anxious or irritable?",B.bdM,B.bej,B.buj,"If anxiety or low mood is there most days, see your doctor. Both hormone and non-hormone treatments can help.",B.aZm,B.bqo)
B.bcl=s(["I feel sad all the time","Depression and menopause","I feel hopeless"],t.s)
B.aZa=s(["depressed","depression","sad","low","hopeless","crying","tearful","down"],t.s)
B.byH=s(["The risk of depression goes up during perimenopause, even for women who have never had it before. It is not a weakness, and it is treatable.","Talking to someone you trust, staying active, keeping a routine, and getting help early all make a difference."],t.s)
B.biE=s([B.Ci,B.a0c,B.lC],t.P)
B.alC=new A.bO("low-mood",B.jC,"I feel low or depressed. What can I do?",B.bcl,B.aZa,B.byH,"See your doctor if you have felt low most days for two weeks or more. If you are thinking about suicide or harming yourself, call or text 9-8-8 any time, or call 911.",B.biE,B.AK)
B.bb3=s(["I have no energy","Always exhausted","Fatigue"],t.s)
B.bke=s(["tired","fatigue","exhausted","energy","drained","sluggish"],t.s)
B.bqq=s(["Tiredness in menopause often comes from broken sleep (night sweats, waking early), plus stress and hormone changes.","It is also worth ruling out other common causes: low iron or anaemia, an underactive thyroid, low vitamin B12, and some medicines. A simple blood test can check these.","Regular meals with protein and fibre, enough water, daylight and gentle activity usually help energy more than rest alone."],t.s)
B.bz2=s([B.a0s,B.Cx,B.Cn],t.P)
B.a4b=new A.fv(null,"b12",18,"b12Blood")
B.bbZ=s([B.pg,B.Ei,B.Ej,B.a4b,B.Eh],t.G)
B.aly=new A.bO("tired",B.jC,"Why am I so tired all the time?",B.bb3,B.bke,B.bqq,"See your doctor if you are tired for more than a few weeks without a clear reason.",B.bz2,B.bbZ)
B.bcC=s(["I feel overwhelmed","Ways to relax"],t.s)
B.bsV=s(["stress","stressed","overwhelmed","relax","calm","tension"],t.s)
B.b0G=s(["Stress can make hot flashes, sleep and mood worse, and midlife often brings a lot of it at once.","A few minutes a day of slow breathing, meditation or yoga, regular movement, time outside, saying no sometimes, and talking things through all help. Small, regular habits work better than an occasional big effort."],t.s)
B.aEF=s([B.Cw,B.Cs],t.P)
B.alW=new A.bO("stress",B.jC,"How can I manage stress?",B.bcC,B.bsV,B.b0G,null,B.aEF,B.Ap)
B.bub=s(["How do I prevent osteoporosis?","Bone loss menopause","Strong bones"],t.s)
B.bjs=s(["bone","bones","osteoporosis","fracture","density"],t.s)
B.aLp=s(["Bone loss speeds up for several years after menopause because oestrogen helps protect bone. That is why osteoporosis is much more common in women after 50.","The basics: enough calcium (mostly from food), vitamin D, enough protein, strength and balance exercise, not smoking and keeping alcohol low."],t.s)
B.bcK=s([B.a0M,B.Ce,B.Ch],t.P)
B.w5=new A.fv(B.ls,null,1,"calcium")
B.Eg=new A.fv(B.op,null,2,"vitaminD")
B.bh1=s([B.w5,B.Eg,B.ph],t.G)
B.alD=new A.bO("bones",B.hY,"How do I look after my bones after menopause?",B.bub,B.bjs,B.aLp,"Ask your doctor about your fracture risk and whether you need a bone density test, especially if you have broken a bone from a minor fall, or a parent broke a hip.",B.bcK,B.bh1)
B.bhR=s(["Should I take calcium?","Calcium foods","Calcium supplement"],t.s)
B.bvF=s(["calcium","dairy","milk","cheese","yogurt"],t.s)
B.beX=s(["Women over 50 need about 1,200 mg of calcium a day in total. Osteoporosis Canada suggests getting it from food first, and only topping up with a supplement if food falls short.","Good sources: milk and fortified plant drinks (about 300 mg a cup), yogurt, cheese, canned salmon or sardines with the bones, tofu made with calcium, almonds, and some greens.","Osteoporosis Canada has a free calcium calculator to estimate what you get from food."],t.s)
B.bur=s([B.Cr,B.a0I],t.P)
B.bd1=s([B.w5],t.G)
B.amg=new A.bO("calcium",B.hY,"How much calcium do I need?",B.bhR,B.bvF,B.beX,"Check with your doctor or pharmacist before starting a calcium supplement, especially if you have had kidney stones.",B.bur,B.bd1)
B.aLd=s(["How much vitamin D do I need?","Vitamin D in winter"],t.s)
B.bhl=s(["vitamin","sun","sunshine","winter","d"],t.s)
B.byh=s(["Vitamin D helps your body use calcium. In Canada the sun is too weak to make enough for much of the year, and few foods have much.","Canada's food guide recommends that adults over 50 take a daily vitamin D supplement of 400 IU, on top of eating foods with vitamin D (milk and fortified plant drinks, fatty fish, eggs). Osteoporosis Canada gives the total daily amount from food and supplements as 600 IU up to age 70 and 800 IU after."],t.s)
B.bii=s([B.Cy,B.uO],t.P)
B.c5l=new A.fv(null,"vitamin_d",19,"vitaminDBlood")
B.b47=s([B.Eg,B.c5l],t.G)
B.ama=new A.bO("vitamin-d",B.hY,"Should I take vitamin D?",B.aLd,B.bhl,B.byh,"Ask your doctor or pharmacist which amount is right for you, especially at higher doses.",B.bii,B.b47)
B.bcw=s(["What is a DEXA scan?","BMD test"],t.s)
B.aZs=s(["dexa","bmd","scan","density","test"],t.s)
B.biw=s(["A bone mineral density (BMD) test is a quick, painless scan that measures bone strength and helps work out your fracture risk.","Osteoporosis Canada suggests it for everyone 70 and over, for women after menopause aged 65 to 69 with one risk factor, and for those 50 to 64 who have broken a bone in a minor fall or have two or more risk factors (such as a parent with a hip fracture, long-term steroid use, low body weight, smoking or early menopause)."],t.s)
B.bBq=s([B.a0J,B.Ce],t.P)
B.alR=new A.bO("bone-density-test",B.hY,"Do I need a bone density test?",B.bcw,B.aZs,B.biw,"Your doctor can tell you whether you should have one and when.",B.bBq,B.bR)
B.bAI=s(["Protein ideas for breakfast","Am I eating enough protein?","Protein for muscle"],t.s)
B.bvI=s(["protein","muscle","breakfast","eggs","beans","meat"],t.s)
B.bmB=s(["Protein helps keep muscle and bone as you age. The basic guideline for adults is 0.8 g per kg of body weight a day, and many experts suggest a little more (about 1.0 to 1.2 g per kg) for women over 50, especially if you are active.","Spreading it across the day helps: some protein at every meal, including breakfast. Greek yogurt, eggs, milk, tofu, beans, lentils, nuts, fish and chicken are all good choices, and Canada's food guide encourages plant proteins often."],t.s)
B.bB1=s([B.a0o,B.lB],t.P)
B.asJ=s([B.w4],t.G)
B.am2=new A.bO("protein",B.hY,"How much protein do I need?",B.bAI,B.bvI,B.bmB,"If you have kidney disease, check with your doctor before eating more protein.",B.bB1,B.asJ)
B.bjZ=s(["Weights after 50","Exercises for bones","How do I keep muscle?"],t.s)
B.bei=s(["strength","weights","resistance","muscle","lifting","gym"],t.s)
B.blc=s(["Yes, it is one of the best things you can do in midlife. Strength work keeps muscle, protects bones, helps balance and blood sugar, and makes everyday tasks easier.","The Canadian guidelines suggest muscle-strengthening on at least two days a week. Bands, light weights, body-weight moves (sit-to-stand, wall push-ups) or Pilates all count. Osteoporosis Canada adds balance work and good posture."],t.s)
B.bhy=s([B.uV,B.Ch,B.uR],t.P)
B.b0H=s([B.ph],t.G)
B.alE=new A.bO("strength-training",B.hY,"Should I do strength training?",B.bjZ,B.bei,B.blc,"If you have osteoporosis or a past fracture, ask for advice on safe moves (a physiotherapist can help).",B.bhy,B.b0H)
B.bg_=s(["Is walking enough?","Exercise guidelines","How active should I be?"],t.s)
B.bgZ=s(["exercise","active","activity","walking","walk","minutes","fitness"],t.s)
B.aQW=s(["The Canadian 24-Hour Movement Guidelines suggest about 150 minutes a week of moderate to vigorous activity (like brisk walking), strength work on two days, and less time sitting. Adults 65+ are also encouraged to do balance exercises.","Walking is a great start. Adding a few hills, some brisk stretches and two short strength sessions a week covers most of it. Every bit counts, even 10 minutes at a time."],t.s)
B.bbe=s([B.uV,B.a08,B.uR],t.P)
B.btS=s([B.w6,B.ph],t.G)
B.alr=new A.bO("how-much-exercise",B.hY,"How much exercise do I need?",B.bg_,B.bgZ,B.aQW,null,B.bbe,B.btS)
B.btg=s(["Heart disease risk after menopause","Protect my heart"],t.s)
B.biv=s(["heart","cardiovascular","heart disease"],t.s)
B.bqX=s(["Yes. Oestrogen helps protect blood vessels, so after menopause the risk of heart disease rises, and it is the leading cause of death for women. LDL cholesterol and blood pressure often go up in these years.","The good news is that most of the risk can be changed: move every day, eat lots of vegetables, fruit, whole grains, beans and nuts, limit salt and saturated fat, don't smoke, keep alcohol low, and know your blood pressure, cholesterol and blood sugar numbers."],t.s)
B.b4d=s([B.uP,B.Cu,B.uN],t.P)
B.a4c=new A.fv(null,"ldl",12,"ldl")
B.a47=new A.fv(B.jx,null,7,"satFat")
B.a48=new A.fv(B.os,null,6,"sodium")
B.bfe=s([B.a4c,B.a47,B.a48],t.G)
B.alO=new A.bO("heart-after-menopause",B.fo,"Does menopause affect my heart?",B.btg,B.biv,B.bqX,"Ask your doctor to check your heart risk, including blood pressure, cholesterol and blood sugar.",B.b4d,B.bfe)
B.bCe=s(["My LDL is high","What foods lower cholesterol?","Cholesterol went up after menopause"],t.s)
B.bb_=s(["cholesterol","ldl","hdl","lipids","triglycerides","statin"],t.s)
B.btF=s(["Cholesterol often rises after menopause. Food can make a real difference, especially:","\u2022 Soluble fibre: oats, barley, beans, lentils, apples, psyllium.\n\u2022 Nuts, about a handful a day.\n\u2022 Soy foods, like tofu, edamame and soy drinks.\n\u2022 Swapping saturated fats (fatty meats, butter, cream, coconut oil) for olive or canola oil, avocado, nuts and seeds.\n\u2022 Foods with added plant sterols.",'Together these make up the "Portfolio diet", developed in Canada. Being active and keeping alcohol low help too.'],t.s)
B.bhq=s([B.a0C,B.uN,B.uP],t.P)
B.c5k=new A.fv(null,"hdl",13,"hdl")
B.b67=s([B.a4c,B.c5k,B.a47,B.pf],t.G)
B.am8=new A.bO("cholesterol",B.fo,"How can I lower my cholesterol with food?",B.bCe,B.bb_,B.btF,"Your doctor looks at cholesterol together with your other risks to decide whether you need medicine. Food changes still help either way.",B.bhq,B.b67)
B.bil=s(["High blood pressure","Does salt raise blood pressure?","Hypertension"],t.s)
B.bvc=s(["pressure","hypertension","salt","sodium"],t.s)
B.bcz=s(["Blood pressure tends to rise after menopause, often without any symptoms, so checking it regularly matters.","Helpful habits: less sodium (most comes from packaged and restaurant food, not the salt shaker), more vegetables, fruit and potassium-rich foods, regular activity, less alcohol, and managing stress. Health Canada suggests adults stay under 2,300 mg of sodium a day."],t.s)
B.bzE=s([B.a0T,B.a0u],t.P)
B.c5h=new A.fv(B.ou,null,11,"potassium")
B.byo=s([B.a48,B.c5h],t.G)
B.amj=new A.bO("blood-pressure",B.fo,"How can I keep my blood pressure healthy?",B.bil,B.bvc,B.bcz,"Have your blood pressure checked at least once a year, or as your doctor suggests.",B.bzE,B.byo)
B.bcq=s(["My blood sugar is high","What is A1C?","Diabetes risk"],t.s)
B.bsU=s(["sugar","glucose","a1c","hba1c","prediabetes","diabetes","insulin"],t.s)
B.baP=s(["Prediabetes means blood sugar is higher than normal but not high enough to be diabetes. Diabetes Canada describes it as an A1C of 6.0 to 6.4% or a fasting glucose of 6.1 to 6.9 mmol/L.","It is a warning sign, and often reversible. Being active (including strength work), more fibre and whole foods, fewer sugary drinks and refined carbs, and losing a little weight if needed can bring it back down."],t.s)
B.bdC=s([B.a0i,B.Cj],t.P)
B.c5j=new A.fv(null,"hba1c",14,"hba1c")
B.c5i=new A.fv(null,"glucose_fasting",15,"glucoseFasting")
B.a4a=new A.fv(B.lt,null,8,"sugar")
B.bBg=s([B.c5j,B.c5i,B.a4a],t.G)
B.alA=new A.bO("blood-sugar",B.fo,"What does prediabetes mean?",B.bcq,B.bsU,B.baP,"Your doctor will tell you how often to recheck. Ask about your diabetes risk if it runs in your family.",B.bdC,B.bBg)
B.aWZ=s(["Chest pain","Heart attack symptoms women","Stroke signs"],t.s)
B.bdv=s(["attack","chest","stroke","emergency","fast"],t.s)
B.bcb=s(["Heart attack signs include chest pain or pressure, discomfort in the arms, neck, jaw, shoulders or back, shortness of breath, nausea, sweating and light-headedness. Women more often have the less typical signs, like breathlessness, nausea or back or jaw pain.","For stroke, remember FAST: Face drooping, Arms can't be raised, Speech slurred or jumbled, Time to call 911."],t.s)
B.beP=s([B.uT,B.oH],t.P)
B.am6=new A.bO("heart-attack-signs",B.fo,"What are the signs of a heart attack or stroke in women?",B.aWZ,B.bdv,B.bcb,"Call 911 right away. Don't drive yourself to hospital.",B.beP,B.bR)
B.boK=s(["Is my result normal?","My lab result is flagged","Understanding lab results"],t.s)
B.bfx=s(["blood","test","results","lab","range","normal","flagged","bloodwork"],t.s)
B.bey=s(["Each lab prints its own reference range: the span where most healthy people fall. A result just outside it isn't always a problem, and one inside it isn't always ideal for you. What matters is the whole picture: your history, symptoms and how results change over time.","Blood work in Daisy keeps your results and their trends, and makes a PDF to bring to your appointment."],t.s)
B.bb1=s([B.Cz],t.P)
B.alt=new A.bO("blood-results",B.fo,"What do my blood test results mean?",B.boK,B.bfx,B.bey,"Your doctor is the right person to explain your results. Write your questions down before the visit.",B.bb1,B.bR)
B.aR_=s(["Thyroid and menopause","What is TSH?","Underactive thyroid"],t.s)
B.byE=s(["thyroid","tsh","hypothyroid","t4"],t.s)
B.brb=s(["Thyroid problems are common in women in midlife, and an underactive thyroid shares many signs with menopause: tiredness, weight gain, low mood, feeling cold, dry skin and hair changes.","A simple blood test (TSH) can check it, and treatment is straightforward if it is low."],t.s)
B.bc4=s([B.Cn,B.a0G],t.P)
B.be1=s([B.Ej],t.G)
B.als=new A.bO("thyroid",B.fo,"Could it be my thyroid?",B.aR_,B.byE,B.brb,"If you have these symptoms, ask your doctor whether a thyroid test makes sense.",B.bc4,B.be1)
B.bBj=s(["Low ferritin","Iron rich foods","Am I anaemic?","Anemia"],t.s)
B.bbg=s(["iron","ferritin","anaemia","anemia","anaemic","anemic","hemoglobin"],t.s)
B.bgN=s(["Heavy periods in perimenopause can lower iron, which can cause tiredness, breathlessness, pale skin and hair loss. After periods stop, women need less iron (about 8 mg a day instead of 18).","Iron is in meat, fish, poultry, beans, lentils, tofu, fortified cereals and dark greens. Eating plant iron with vitamin C (peppers, citrus, tomatoes) helps you absorb it, and tea or coffee with meals lowers it."],t.s)
B.aZb=s([B.Cx,B.a0S],t.P)
B.bCr=s([B.Eh,B.pg,B.Ei],t.G)
B.alY=new A.bO("iron",B.fo,"Do I need more iron?",B.bBj,B.bbg,B.bgN,"Don't take iron supplements without a blood test: too much iron can be harmful. Ask your doctor if you are tired or have heavy periods.",B.aZb,B.bCr)
B.bb9=s(["Low B12","B12 after 50"],t.s)
B.bdq=s(["b12","cobalamin","tingling","numbness","pins"],t.s)
B.be9=s(["Vitamin B12 keeps nerves and blood healthy. As we get older the body absorbs less from food, and some medicines (like metformin and stomach-acid reducers) lower it further.","It is found in meat, fish, eggs, milk and fortified plant drinks and cereals. Vegans and many people over 50 rely on fortified foods or a supplement."],t.s)
B.bmM=s([B.Cm],t.P)
B.a49=new A.fv(B.uC,null,10,"vitaminB12")
B.aZz=s([B.a49,B.a4b],t.G)
B.alG=new A.bO("b12",B.fo,"Do I need vitamin B12?",B.bb9,B.bdq,B.be9,"Tiredness, tingling or numbness can be signs of low B12: ask your doctor about a blood test.",B.bmM,B.aZz)
B.bun=s(["Best diet for menopause","Healthy eating in midlife","Menopause foods","What can I eat to help with symptoms?"],t.s)
B.bba=s(["diet","eat","eating","nutrition","meals","healthy"],t.s)
B.bj_=s(["There is no special menopause diet, but some things matter more now: protein at each meal for muscle, calcium and vitamin D for bones, fibre and healthy fats for the heart, and lots of colourful vegetables and fruit.","Canada's food guide is a good simple pattern: half your plate vegetables and fruit, a quarter whole grains, a quarter protein foods, with water as your drink of choice.","Limiting alcohol, caffeine and very spicy food can help if they trigger your hot flashes."],t.s)
B.baK=s([B.lB,B.uO],t.P)
B.bpc=s([B.w4,B.w5,B.pf],t.G)
B.alz=new A.bO("menopause-diet",B.f_,"What should I eat during menopause?",B.bun,B.bba,B.bj_,null,B.baK,B.bpc)
B.bkz=s(["High fiber foods","Am I eating enough fiber?"],t.s)
B.blj=s(["fibre","fiber","whole","grains","oats","beans"],t.s)
B.biC=s(["Most Canadians eat only about half the fibre they need. Women are advised to aim for about 21 to 25 g a day.","Fibre helps digestion, keeps you full, and helps cholesterol and blood sugar. Good sources: oats, whole grain bread and pasta, beans, lentils, chickpeas, vegetables, fruit with the skin, nuts and seeds. Add it slowly and drink more water to avoid bloating."],t.s)
B.aWY=s([B.Cf,B.a0l],t.P)
B.alq=new A.bO("fibre",B.f_,"How much fibre do I need?",B.bkz,B.blj,B.biC,null,B.aWY,B.PP)
B.bCq=s(["Phytoestrogens","Is soy safe?","Flaxseed for hot flashes"],t.s)
B.bf1=s(["soy","soya","tofu","edamame","phytoestrogens","isoflavones","flax","flaxseed"],t.s)
B.bli=s(["Soy foods contain plant compounds (isoflavones) that act a little like weak oestrogen. Studies show a small effect on hot flashes for some women, but results are mixed.","Soy foods like tofu, edamame and soy drinks are a healthy protein either way, and are considered safe as part of a normal diet. Supplements with concentrated isoflavones are less well studied."],t.s)
B.baM=s([B.Ck,B.lB],t.P)
B.am_=new A.bO("soy",B.f_,"Does soy help with menopause?",B.bCq,B.bf1,B.bli,"If you have had breast cancer, ask your doctor before taking soy supplements.",B.baM,B.bR)
B.bh5=s(["Fish oil","Fatty fish","Omega 3 foods"],t.s)
B.bm2=s(["omega","omega3","fish","salmon","oil","walnuts","chia"],t.s)
B.bcT=s(["Omega-3 fats are good for the heart and brain. Eating fatty fish like salmon, trout, sardines or mackerel twice a week is a common suggestion.","Plant sources (ground flax, chia, walnuts, canola oil, soy) give a different omega-3 called ALA; women need about 1.1 g a day."],t.s)
B.boc=s([B.uN,B.lB],t.P)
B.c5g=new A.fv(B.or,null,5,"omega3")
B.bAh=s([B.c5g],t.G)
B.alv=new A.bO("omega-3",B.f_,"Do I need omega-3s?",B.bh5,B.bm2,B.bcT,"Check with your doctor or pharmacist before taking fish oil capsules if you take blood thinners.",B.boc,B.bAh)
B.bxB=s(["Does caffeine make hot flashes worse?","Caffeine and sleep"],t.s)
B.bc1=s(["coffee","caffeine","tea","espresso","energy drink"],t.s)
B.bCw=s(["Health Canada says most adults can safely have up to 400 mg of caffeine a day, about three 8 oz (237 ml) cups of brewed coffee.","In menopause, caffeine can trigger hot flashes, palpitations and bladder urgency, and it can disturb sleep for many hours. Having it only before noon, or trying half-caf, helps many women."],t.s)
B.btk=s([B.a0m,B.uS],t.P)
B.alw=new A.bO("caffeine",B.f_,"How much coffee is OK?",B.bxB,B.bc1,B.bCw,null,B.btk,B.bR)
B.be8=s(["Is wine bad for me?","Alcohol and menopause","A glass of wine"],t.s)
B.bdT=s(["alcohol","wine","beer","drink","drinks","drinking","cocktail"],t.s)
B.bBk=s(["Canada's Guidance on Alcohol and Health (2023) says less is better. At two standard drinks or fewer a week you are likely to avoid harms. At three to six, the risk of several cancers (including breast cancer) goes up, and at seven or more the risk of heart disease and stroke rises significantly.","A standard drink is a 142 ml (5 oz) glass of 12% wine, a 341 ml bottle of 5% beer, or 43 ml of 40% spirits. Alcohol can also trigger hot flashes and break up sleep."],t.s)
B.aWV=s([B.a0r,B.uS],t.P)
B.am0=new A.bO("alcohol",B.f_,"How much alcohol is safe?",B.be8,B.bdT,B.bBk,null,B.aWV,B.bR)
B.bqr=s(["Am I drinking enough?","Hydration"],t.s)
B.bum=s(["water","hydration","hydrated","thirsty","fluids"],t.s)
B.bq5=s(["There is no single number: needs change with heat, activity and hot flashes. A good guide is drinking regularly through the day so your urine is pale yellow. Food (fruit, vegetables, soups) counts too.","Canada's food guide suggests making water your drink of choice. If bladder leaks or night-time bathroom trips are a problem, drink steadily during the day and a little less in the evening rather than cutting back overall."],t.s)
B.bdc=s([B.uO,B.uU],t.P)
B.alK=new A.bO("water",B.f_,"How much water should I drink?",B.bqr,B.bum,B.bq5,null,B.bdc,B.bR)
B.bnO=s(["Sweet cravings","Snacking at night","Always hungry"],t.s)
B.btm=s(["craving","cravings","sweet","sweets","snack","snacking","hungry","chocolate"],t.s)
B.aQZ=s(["Cravings often come from tiredness, stress, long gaps between meals, or meals low in protein and fibre.","Regular meals with protein, fibre and some healthy fat keep blood sugar steadier. Having a planned snack (yogurt and fruit, nuts, hummus and veggies) helps, and so does better sleep. Health Canada suggests limiting added sugars."],t.s)
B.bnS=s([B.Cj,B.lB],t.P)
B.bzh=s([B.a4a,B.w4,B.pf],t.G)
B.am5=new A.bO("sugar-cravings",B.f_,"Why do I crave sugar?",B.bnO,B.btm,B.aQZ,null,B.bnS,B.bzh)
B.bfg=s(["Which vitamins should I take?","Do I need supplements?"],t.s)
B.bcn=s(["multivitamin","multivitamins","vitamins","supplements"],t.s)
B.aXe=s(["Most nutrients are best from food, and a varied diet covers most of what you need. A few are harder to get from food after 50:","\u2022 Vitamin D: Health Canada recommends a daily 400 IU supplement for everyone over 50.\n\u2022 Vitamin B12: absorbed less well with age; fortified foods or a supplement can help.\n\u2022 Calcium: only if food falls short of about 1,200 mg a day.","A basic multivitamin for adults over 50 is a simple way to cover vitamin D and B12 for some women. More is not better: high doses of some vitamins and minerals can be harmful."],t.s)
B.aZi=s([B.Cy,B.Cr,B.Cm],t.P)
B.bfY=s([B.Eg,B.a49,B.w5],t.G)
B.amd=new A.bO("multivitamin",B.f_,"Should I take a multivitamin?",B.bfg,B.bcn,B.aXe,"Ask your doctor or pharmacist before starting supplements, especially if you take medicines.",B.aZi,B.bfY)
B.asy=s(["Magnesium for sleep","Magnesium foods"],t.s)
B.QF=s(["magnesium"],t.s)
B.bhe=s(["Magnesium is needed for muscles, nerves and bones. Women over 30 need about 320 mg a day, which most people can get from nuts, seeds, beans, whole grains, leafy greens and dark chocolate.","Magnesium supplements are popular for sleep and cramps, but the evidence is limited. High doses from supplements can cause diarrhoea."],t.s)
B.bfE=s([B.a0U],t.P)
B.c5m=new A.fv(B.uB,null,9,"magnesium")
B.bfr=s([B.c5m],t.G)
B.amf=new A.bO("magnesium",B.f_,"Should I take magnesium?",B.asy,B.QF,B.bhe,"Ask your doctor or pharmacist first, especially if you have kidney problems or take other medicines.",B.bfE,B.bfr)
B.bqn=s(["Bladder leaks","Incontinence menopause","I always need to pee","Pelvic floor"],t.s)
B.bfz=s(["leak","leaks","leaking","bladder","incontinence","pee","urine","pelvic","kegel"],t.s)
B.aZc=s(["Bladder leaks and urgency become more common after menopause, as lower oestrogen and weaker pelvic floor muscles affect bladder control. It is common, but not something you just have to live with.","Pelvic floor exercises (Kegels) done daily help a lot, especially for leaks when you cough, laugh or sneeze. The Pelvic floor trainer in Daisy guides you through them. Less caffeine and alcohol helps urgency."],t.s)
B.bcg=s([B.uU,B.a0R,B.a0p],t.P)
B.ame=new A.bO("bladder-leaks",B.oI,"Why do I leak when I cough or sneeze?",B.bqn,B.bfz,B.aZc,"Ask your doctor about it, and about a pelvic floor physiotherapist. Vaginal oestrogen can also help.",B.bcg,B.bR)
B.asq=s(["UTI after menopause","Burning when I pee"],t.s)
B.bcx=s(["uti","utis","infection","infections","burning","cystitis"],t.s)
B.bf2=s(["After menopause, thinner tissue and changes in vaginal bacteria make urinary tract infections more likely.","Drinking enough, not holding urine for long, and peeing after sex help. For repeat infections, vaginal oestrogen has good evidence for lowering how often they happen."],t.s)
B.bij=s([B.a0D,B.uU],t.P)
B.alS=new A.bO("utis",B.oI,"Why do I keep getting bladder infections?",B.asq,B.bcx,B.bf2,"See your doctor for burning, urgency or cloudy urine. Get care quickly if you have fever, back or side pain, or blood in your urine.",B.bij,B.bR)
B.be3=s(["Painful sex","Vaginal itching","Dryness down there"],t.s)
B.bbk=s(["vaginal","dryness","painful","sex","intercourse","itching","gsm"],t.s)
B.bpk=s(["Vaginal dryness, itching and discomfort during sex are very common after menopause and, unlike hot flashes, often don't go away on their own.","Vaginal moisturisers (used a few times a week) and lubricants (used during sex) help many women. Low-dose vaginal oestrogen is very effective and considered safe for most women, as very little reaches the rest of the body."],t.s)
B.byg=s([B.Ct,B.a0H],t.P)
B.alL=new A.bO("vaginal-dryness",B.oI,"What helps with vaginal dryness?",B.be3,B.bbk,B.bpk,"Talk to your doctor: it is a common, treatable problem and worth raising.",B.byg,B.bR)
B.ble=s(["Low libido","Not interested in sex"],t.s)
B.brd=s(["libido","desire","drive","intimacy"],t.s)
B.bbo=s(["Lower desire is common in midlife. Hormone changes, vaginal dryness or discomfort, tiredness, poor sleep, stress, mood, relationships and some medicines can all play a part.","Treating dryness or pain, better sleep, and talking openly with your partner often help."],t.s)
B.bfc=s([B.Ct,B.uQ],t.P)
B.alp=new A.bO("libido",B.oI,"Why is my sex drive lower?",B.ble,B.brd,B.bbo,"If it bothers you, mention it to your doctor; there are options, and they hear about it often.",B.bfc,B.bR)
B.bew=s(["Should I take HRT?","Risks of hormone therapy","MHT","Estrogen therapy"],t.s)
B.bf7=s(["hrt","hormone","hormones","therapy","mht","estrogen","oestrogen","progesterone","patch"],t.s)
B.brq=s(["For women within ten years of menopause, Canadian experts (SOGC) and the North American Menopause Society say the benefits of hormone therapy for bothersome symptoms outweigh the risks. It is the most effective treatment for hot flashes and night sweats, and it also protects bone.","Risks depend on your age, health and the type you use. Oestrogen through the skin (patch or gel) has a lower risk of blood clots than pills. If you still have a uterus you also need a progestogen to protect its lining."],t.s)
B.bkO=s([B.a0P,B.a0d,B.a0k],t.P)
B.alx=new A.bO("hrt-safe",B.oJ,"Is hormone therapy (HRT) safe?",B.bew,B.bf7,B.brq,"Whether it is right for you is a decision to make with your doctor, based on your own and your family's health history.",B.bkO,B.bR)
B.bid=s(["Non-hormonal treatment for hot flashes","Alternatives to HRT"],t.s)
B.bdh=s(["non-hormonal","alternative","alternatives","without hormones","gabapentin","fezolinetant"],t.s)
B.aX1=s(["There are several prescription options that are not hormones and can reduce hot flashes, including some antidepressants in low doses, gabapentin, and newer medicines made specifically for hot flashes.","CBT and clinical hypnosis also have good evidence, and they have no side effects."],t.s)
B.bd4=s([B.Co,B.a0z],t.P)
B.alN=new A.bO("non-hormonal",B.oJ,"What can I take if I can't use hormones?",B.bid,B.bdh,B.aX1,"Your doctor can explain which might suit you.",B.bd4,B.bR)
B.b0v=s(["Compounded hormones","Natural hormones"],t.s)
B.bcE=s(["bioidentical","compounded","natural","body-identical"],t.s)
B.beo=s(['"Bioidentical" means hormones with the same structure as the body\'s own. Some approved products in Canada are like this (estradiol patches and gels, micronized progesterone).','Custom-compounded "bioidentical" mixes made by some pharmacies are not tested or regulated the same way, so their strength and safety are less certain. SOGC recommends approved products instead.'],t.s)
B.bBF=s([B.a0h],t.P)
B.alB=new A.bO("bioidentical",B.oJ,"What are bioidentical hormones?",B.b0v,B.bcE,B.beo,null,B.bBF,B.bR)
B.blu=s(["Herbal remedies for menopause","Evening primrose oil","Natural supplements for hot flashes"],t.s)
B.brs=s(["supplement","supplements","herbal","cohosh","primrose","ginseng","clover","remedies","natural"],t.s)
B.bgm=s(['Many supplements are sold for menopause (black cohosh, red clover, evening primrose, ginseng and others). Good studies show little or no benefit for most, and "natural" doesn\'t always mean safe: black cohosh has been linked to rare liver problems.',"Products vary a lot in what they contain. In Canada, look for an NPN (Natural Product Number) on the label, which means Health Canada has reviewed it."],t.s)
B.bbx=s([B.Ck],t.P)
B.alu=new A.bO("supplements",B.oJ,"Do supplements like black cohosh work?",B.blu,B.brs,B.bgm,"Tell your doctor or pharmacist about any supplement, as some interact with medicines.",B.bbx,B.bR)
B.bBE=s(["What should I ask my doctor?","Preparing for an appointment","My doctor doesn't listen"],t.s)
B.bgE=s(["appointment","doctor","visit","prepare","questions","find","specialist","clinic","practitioner","gynecologist","gynaecologist"],t.s)
B.brl=s(["It helps to go prepared: write down your symptoms, how often they happen and how much they affect you, your period dates, medicines and supplements, and your questions.","Bring it up early in the visit, and say clearly what you want help with. The Journal, blood work PDF and Day summary in Daisy can help you remember details.","The Menopause Foundation of Canada has a free guide to taking charge of your care, and a list to help find a menopause-informed practitioner."],t.s)
B.bzP=s([B.Cz,B.a0K],t.P)
B.amh=new A.bO("talk-to-doctor",B.uW,"How do I talk to my doctor about menopause?",B.bBE,B.bgE,B.brl,null,B.bzP,B.bR)
B.bgz=s(["Breast cancer screening","Cancer screening after 50"],t.s)
B.bhx=s(["mammogram","breast","screening","cancer","pap","colon"],t.s)
B.bbr=s(["Screening finds some cancers early, when they are easiest to treat. SOGC suggests menopause is a good time to make a plan with your doctor for breast, colon and cervical cancer screening.","Breast screening programs (mammograms) are different in each province and territory, and your own family history or dense breasts can change what is right for you."],t.s)
B.bfV=s([B.Cv],t.P)
B.amb=new A.bO("mammogram",B.uW,"Do I need a mammogram?",B.bgz,B.bhx,B.bbr,"Ask your doctor or your provincial screening program what you are due for. See your doctor any time you notice a breast lump or change.",B.bfV,B.bR)
B.bbt=s(["Is this an emergency?","Should I go to the ER?"],t.s)
B.bbn=s(["emergency","urgent","er","hospital","911","nurse","811"],t.s)
B.bg0=s(["Call 911 for chest pain or pressure, trouble breathing, signs of stroke (face drooping, weak arm, slurred speech), fainting, or very heavy bleeding.","If you are thinking about suicide, call or text 9-8-8 any time.","For other worries, in most provinces you can call 811 to talk to a registered nurse for free, any time of day."],t.s)
B.buz=s([B.uT,B.oH,B.Ci],t.P)
B.alT=new A.bO("when-urgent",B.uW,"When should I get help right away?",B.bbt,B.bbn,B.bg0,null,B.buz,B.bR)
